---
// /privacy-policy/ — noindex until the real data practices are documented and counsel has read it.
//
// THIS IS NOT A TEMPLATE POLICY WITH THE COMPANY NAME SWAPPED IN, and it must not become one. A
// privacy policy is a set of factual claims about what an organisation actually does with
// personal data; a generic one is simply inaccurate, and the accurate version is the one that
// holds up when someone asks. So the sections below state only what is verifiable from this
// codebase — the estimate form's four fields — and every question that needs an answer from the
// business is marked in the page as unanswered rather than filled with boilerplate.
//
// What is still needed: analytics and ad pixels, call tracking (CallRail is planned), which CRM
// receives leads, retention periods, SMS/TCPA consent language for the phone field, and whether
// any of this is shared with lead-buying partners. Then counsel review.
import PageShell from "../layouts/PageShell.astro";
import { MARKET_LIST, NATIONAL } from "../data/markets.js";
---
<PageShell
  hero={false}
  badges={false}
  title="Privacy Policy | Coldstream Exteriors"
  description="How Coldstream Exteriors handles the information you give us through this website."
  canonical="/privacy-policy/"
  noindex={true}
  cta={false}
  eyebrow="Legal"
  heading="Privacy policy"
  intro="What we collect through this website, and what we do with it."
>
  <section>
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <div class="unsourced">
        <strong>Draft — not yet in force</strong>
        <p>
          This policy is incomplete and has not been reviewed by counsel. The sections marked
          below need answers from the business before it can be published, and the page is kept
          out of the search index until then.
        </p>
      </div>

      <h2>What we collect</h2>
      <p>
        The estimate form on this site asks for four things: your name, your phone number, your
        ZIP code, and which service you are enquiring about. Those four fields are the only
        personal information this website asks you to provide.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you call one of the numbers on this site, you are giving us your phone number and
        whatever you tell us on the call.
      </p>

      <div class="unsourced">
        <strong>Unanswered</strong>
        <p>
          Whether this site runs analytics, advertising pixels or call-tracking software — and if
          so, which — is not yet documented. Each of those collects information automatically and
          has to be disclosed here by name.
        </p>
      </div>

      <h2>What we use it with</h2>
      <p>
        We use what you give us to contact you about the work you asked about — to call you back,
        arrange an inspection, and send you a quote.
      </p>

      <div class="unsourced">
        <strong>Unanswered</strong>
        <p>
          Which systems your details are stored in, how long they are kept, who else receives
          them, and what consent your phone number carries for calls and texts. None of these can
          be answered from the website alone, and none of them will be guessed at here.
        </p>
      </div>

      <h2>Contacting us about your information</h2>
      <p>
        To ask what we hold about you, or to ask us to delete it, call the office for your area:
      </p>
      <ul>
        {MARKET_LIST.map((m) => (
          <li>{m.name} — {m.office.street}, {m.office.city}, {m.office.state} {m.office.zip}. <a href={m.telHref}>{m.phone}</a></li>
        ))}
        <li>Anywhere else — <a href={NATIONAL.telHref}>{NATIONAL.phone}</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>
</PageShell>
